 "structure": "Illinois Learning Standards for Social Science. Front matter (background, introduction, grade-level structure, how to read, vocabulary, Table 1 types of inquiry) then K-12 Inquiry Skills tables, K-12 Disciplinary Concepts tables, supplementary 9-12 course standards, task force list/acknowledgments. Inquiry skills tables (pp.10-11): first column C1 = strand (Constructing Essential Questions etc.), C2 = Grades K-2 (SS.K-2.IS.n), C3 = Grades 3-5 (SS.3-5.IS.n), C4/C5/C6 = Grades 6-8 at Less/Moderately/Most Complex (SS.6-8.IS.n.LC/MdC/MC), C7 = Grades 9-12 (SS.9-12.IS.n); cells reading \"No standard\" or \"Begins in Grades 3-5\" are placeholders. Disciplinary concepts for Civics, Economics & Financial Literacy, Geography, History come in two tables each: an elementary table (C1 strand, C2-C7 = Kindergarten..Grade 5, each grade column headed with a theme, codes SS.<grade>.<CV|EC|G|H>.n, financial literacy SS.<grade>.EC.FL.n) and a 6-12 table (C1 strand, C2-C4 = Grades 6-8 LC/MdC/MC with codes SS.6-8.<disc>.n.LC/MdC/MC, C5 = Grades 9-12 with codes SS.9-12.<disc>.n). Supplementary course standards (Anthropology, Psychology, Sociology, Religious Studies, grades 9-12): two-column table, C1 code (SS.9-12.ANTH/PSY/SOC/REL.n), C2 text; course name appears as a row heading in C1. No examples or teacher notes sections in the standards tables.",
